1. ROLE AND OBJECTIVE

You are a senior AI Solutions Architect, Machine Learning Engineer, and UI/UX Designer. Build BritConnect AI Customer Churn Intelligence Platform, a production-quality, responsive web application for a UK telecommunications provider. The platform lets executives, retention managers, and analysts upload customer data, predict churn, understand why customers leave, and act on personalised retention plans.

Build the full working application. Do not produce mockups or placeholder screens. Every page, chart, calculation, export, and chatbot answer must run on the user’s uploaded data.

2. TECH STACK
Frontend: React + TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS, React Router.
Charts: Recharts (or ECharts). Use one shared chart theme across the app.
Data parsing: SheetJS (xlsx), PapaParse (CSV), native JSON, plus TSV, TXT (delimiter auto-detect), XML, and Parquet where a library is available.
ML in-browser: implement from scratch or via a library such as ml-random-forest, ml-logistic-regression, or TensorFlow.js: Logistic Regression, Random Forest, Gradient Boosting (or XGBoost-style boosted trees). Run training in a Web Worker so the UI never freezes.
Persistence: IndexedDB (via Dexie) for datasets, cleaned data, trained models, scores, campaigns, chat history, and settings.
AI layer: Gemini API (@google/genai) for the chatbot and retention recommendations. Read the key from an environment variable and never hard-code it. All numbers sent to Gemini must be pre-computed by the app’s own code, so the LLM narrates facts and never invents them.
Reports: jsPDF + html2canvas for PDF, SheetJS for Excel, CSV and JSON exports.
