Target variable: Churn Flag. If it is missing, derive it from Churn Status. If the two disagree, flag the row in the validation report.

Critical leakage rule: Churn Status, Churn Date, Churn Reason, Churn Flag, and Monthly Revenue At Risk GBP must never be used as model inputs. Churn Reason and Churn Date exist only after a customer has left. Customer ID is an identifier only. Lifetime Revenue GBP and Tenure Months are checked for leakage (churned customers stop accumulating revenue), and the app shows the user a warning with a toggle to include or exclude them. The default is to keep Tenure Months and exclude Lifetime Revenue GBP from training while using it for value weighting.

Schema flexibility: match uploaded columns to the schema using fuzzy name matching (case, spaces, underscores, synonyms). If columns differ, show a column-mapping screen where users map their columns to the expected fields. Unmapped optional columns are skipped gracefully, and the app still works with a reduced feature set as long as a churn target and Customer ID exist.

