5.8 Retention Recommendations (AI-generated)

For an individual customer, a segment, or the top-N at-risk customers, generate plans using Gemini with a structured JSON schema and the app’s computed evidence. Every recommendation must include:

Diagnosis and evidence: the specific drivers with real values (e.g. “3 outages and 2 complaints in 12 months; resolution time 41 h versus a 18 h segment average; contract ends in 2 months; competitor offer received”).
Personalised actions: concrete offers or interventions matched to the drivers (proactive service credit, plan right-sizing when usage nears or exceeds allowance, loyalty-contract incentive with a discount, payment-plan support, engineer visit, executive escalation, competitor price-match, upgrade or downgrade).
Priority (P1 immediate within 48 h, P2 within 2 weeks, P3 within 30–60 days) and an owner (e.g. Retention Team, Network Ops, Billing, CX).
Step-by-step implementation plan with channel (phone, SMS, email, app), timing, script outline or message theme, and offer guardrails (maximum discount, approval needed).
Expected business impact: estimated save-rate range, retained monthly and annual revenue (£), cost of the intervention, net ROI, and payback period. State all assumptions, and make the assumptions editable (save rate, offer cost, margin) with the figures recalculating live.
Measurable KPIs with baseline, target, and review date (e.g. “Churn rate of this segment: 24% → 18% in 90 days”, “Repeat complaints: 2.1 → 1.0”, “Save-offer acceptance ≥ 30%”, “NPS +8 points”).
Risks and compliance notes: UK GDPR and PECR consent for marketing contact, Ofcom rules on fair treatment and contract-ending notifications, and no use of protected characteristics (Gender, Age) as the basis for differential offers. Do not recommend actions that are discriminatory.
A confidence level with the rationale, and a clear label separating data-backed claims from assumptions.

Prompting rules for Gemini: use only supplied facts, never invent figures, return valid JSON that the UI renders into formatted cards, handle API failures with a retry and a rule-based fallback recommendation engine (so the feature still works offline). Provide Approve, Edit, and Send to Campaign Tracker buttons, and export plans to PDF, Word-compatible text, and CSV.

