6. ACCURACY AND ROBUSTNESS REQUIREMENTS
All calculations are deterministic, centralised, and unit-tested: churn rate = churned ÷ total customers in the filtered set, ARPU = mean Monthly Charge, revenue at risk = defined consistently everywhere, and a metrics glossary page explains every KPI formula.
Guard against divide-by-zero, NaN, and empty filters (show “No data for this selection” with a reset option). Suppress or flag percentages for groups with n < 30.
Never leak the target into features, never fit encoders or scalers on test data, and apply identical transformations at scoring time.
Handle files up to roughly 200k rows smoothly (chunked parsing, workers, virtualised tables) and show progress indicators. Errors are shown in friendly language with suggested fixes and never as raw stack traces. Add an error boundary around each page.
Add a disclosure panel on the model page stating limitations: correlation is not causation, performance depends on data quality, and predictions support rather than replace human judgement.
Data stays in the browser by default. State clearly in the UI which data (aggregated statistics only) is sent to Gemini, and offer a “Do not send customer-level data to AI” privacy toggle (on by default) that restricts the chatbot and recommendations to aggregates and anonymised IDs unless the user opts in.
