Notes on how I shaped this for your data:

Leakage protection is built in. Your dictionary contains post-churn fields (Churn Date, Churn Reason, Churn Status) and Monthly Revenue At Risk, which would let a model “cheat”. The prompt blocks them from training and uses Churn Reason only for descriptive analysis.
Tenure Months and Lifetime Revenue GBP can also leak, because churned customers stop accumulating both. The prompt flags this with a toggle so you can decide.
UK-specific details are included: GBP formatting, dd/mm/yyyy date parsing, UK Nation analysis, and UK GDPR, PECR, and Ofcom compliance notes in the recommendations.
Fairness: Gender and Age are available for analysis, but the recommendations are instructed not to base offers on them.